INT. PAWNSHOP BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Shelves of guitars and watches. A single bare bulb. A card table.

A MAN IN A BEIGE TRENCHCOAT (40s) sits across from GINO FALCONE (50s, shirt sleeves rolled, gold chain), who shuffles a deck. Behind them, a lanky kid, TREVOR PRICE (20s, hoodie), leans on a locker, picking at a thumbnail.

GINO
You're late.

MAN IN TRENCHCOAT
Traffic.

GINO
There's no traffic.

MAN IN TRENCHCOAT
That's what makes it suspicious.

Trevor snorts. Gino deals three cards face down.

GINO
Name's Gino. This is Trevor. What do we call you?

MAN IN TRENCHCOAT
Ellis.

GINO
Ellis what?

ELLIS
Just Ellis.

Gino flips a card. Ace of spades. He grins.

GINO
Ellis, you know why you're here?

ELLIS
You tell me.

GINO
Because you owe.

ELLIS
I know what I owe.

GINO
Then pay.

Ellis reaches into his coat. Trevor straightens, hand drifting to his waistband. Gino raises a palm: easy. Ellis slowly lays a thick envelope on the table.

ELLIS
Count it.

Gino thumbs through the bills, nods once, and slides the envelope under the table.

GINO
Pleasure doing business.
